--api-key: deny by default, allow liveness paths.

The old guard authenticated only the /v1, /v2, /inference and /cohere
prefixes, which left /tokenize, /detokenize, /metrics, /docs and
/server_info answerable without the key -- /tokenize renders arbitrary
text through the model's chat template, so that is template exposure,
not just metadata. The --api-key help text warned about exactly this
class of hole. Today only loopback binding stands between those routes
and the network.

With --api-key bound, every path now requires the bearer token except
/health, /ping, /load and /version -- the allowlist liveness probes and
load balancers need, nothing else. A route added tomorrow is guarded by
default instead of staying open until someone remembers to extend a
prefix list. Prometheus scrapers that cannot carry the key belong on a
separate listener, not on this allowlist. The --api-key help text now
describes the allowlist instead of the old prefix limitation.

The allowlist is matched on the path with any trailing slash removed.
This middleware runs ahead of the router, so /health/ never reaches
FastAPI's redirect_slashes and an exact-match test would answer a
liveness probe configured with a trailing slash with 401.

